+
+**Two scales, one vector (Alec, 2026-10-04).** Alec's concern: order-0
+concepts are mereological and higher-order concepts distributional, "a bit at
+odds; the order-0 distribution might be difficult to overcome to create the
+metric determined by the contextual distribution." Bands were considered and
+rejected: higher-order concepts have no form, so a form band is a strict
+segmentation they cannot fill, and inside a meaning band nothing keeps
+vectors apart; the collapse recurs. Alec: "give parts the low order bits of
+the spatial encoding ... the same way that positional encoding is used to
+make minor deviations between vectors in a meaningful space ... and use
+wholes (context) as the major metric of conceptual space (the higher order
+bits)."
+
+The code is one vector at two scales, c = M + ε·F: M the context term (the
+normalized recency-weighted mean of the roots of the word's occurrence rows,
+detached), F the form term (the evidence-weighted sum of its percept-concept
+rows, live), ε small.
+
+- Similarity is M's: cosine is dominated by context; the form perturbs it at
+  order ε, as position perturbs a token embedding. Synonyms sit together,
+  differing in the low bits.
+- Identity is F's: codes with identical contexts differ by εF and never
+  coincide. The pressure that keeps meaning vectors apart comes from bits
+  that are always distinct; nothing learns it. The permissible collapse is of
+  the high bits only.
+- Higher orders have no form and need none: under coordinate-wise
+  composition, (M₁+εF₁)∘(M₂+εF₂) = M₁∘M₂ + ε(M₁∘F₂+F₁∘M₂) + ε²F₁∘F₂, the
+  constituents' meanings composed with identity residue at order ε.
+
+**ε from evidence against prior (recommended; no constant).** With n the
+word's stored occurrences, c = (n·M + F)/(n + 1): a new word is all form; a
+word seen twice (XOR_grammar) is one-third form and reads XOR with weights of
+order 3; a word seen ten thousand times is context in all but its last
+digits. The center between parts and wholes moves toward the wholes as they
+accumulate. The alternative is a fixed ε, as positional encodings use; it
+must not be made tiny, since the XOR reader needs weights of order 1/ε to
+read identity. For Codex, item 1: one vector, two scales, c = (n·M + F)/(n+1).
